#
# onyx_susfs.fragment - ReSukiSU + SUSFS, applied only when enable_susfs=true
#
# These symbols only exist once build-onyx.yml has applied
#   kernel_patches/KernelSU/10_enable_susfs_for_ksu.patch
# from susfs4ksu (branch gki-android15-6.6, tracked at its branch head -- not
# pinned, so upstream fixes land without editing this repository). If the patch
# stops applying, olddefconfig drops both symbols below and gate 3 fails the
# build -- which is the intended behaviour: a silently dead SUSFS is worse than
# a failed build.
#
# NOTE on the branch name: this tree is 6.6.142 on branch `seventeen`, and
# susfs4ksu has no android17-6.6 branch. Its only 6.6 branch is
# `gki-android15-6.6`. That patch was verified to apply to 6.6.142 anyway:
# 19 hunks, 0 failures, exit 0, with exactly one hunk (fs/proc/base.c #4)
# landing at fuzz 1. The build-onyx.yml step records the actual commit it used
# in SUSFS_STATUS, and gate 3 fails the build if the symbols go missing -- so a
# future upstream change that breaks this is loud, not silent.
#
# Only the two entry points are listed. Every sub-option of CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS is
# "bool ... default y" in that Kconfig, so enabling the parent enables all of
# them. The list below was read out of that patch at the time of writing, so
# the count is checked rather than guessed:
#
#   KSU_SUSFS_SUS_PATH                   KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_UNAME
#   KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MOUNT                  KSU_SUSFS_ENABLE_LOG
#   KSU_SUSFS_SUS_KSTAT                  KSU_SUSFS_HIDE_KSU_SUSFS_SYMBOLS
#   KSU_SUSFS_OPEN_REDIRECT              KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_CMDLINE_OR_BOOTCONFIG
#   KSU_SUSFS_SUS_MAP
#
# (9 sub-options, as of commit a0f9c59e. The 6.6.82 tree's copy of this file
# said "all ten" while listing nine; the count there was never verifiable
# because susfs4ksu was only present at CI time. Here it was checked once --
# since the branch is no longer pinned, treat the list as documentation and
# re-check it if SUSFS behaviour changes.)
#
# gki-clo instead appended eight symbols in a blind loop. Three of them --
# KSU_SUSFS_HAS_MAGIC_MOUNT,
# KSU_SUSFS_AUTO_ADD_SUS_KSU_DEFAULT_KSU_DENYLIST and
# KSU_SUSFS_SUS_OVERLAYFS -- do not exist on this branch at all, and gate 3
# rejected them:
#   -KSU_SUSFS_HAS_MAGIC_MOUNT y
#   -KSU_SUSFS_AUTO_ADD_SUS_KSU_DEFAULT_KSU_DENYLIST y
#   -KSU_SUSFS_SUS_OVERLAYFS y
#
# CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SUS_PATH is a bool, not a string. An earlier revision here
# set it to "/system/susfs" and gate 2 rejected that with
#   warning: symbol value '"/system/susfs"' invalid for KSU_SUSFS_SUS_PATH
#
# Both mistakes came from configuring symbols this repository cannot see.
# Keeping the fragment to the two symbols whose semantics are actually known
# makes it immune to the next susfs4ksu rename.
#
# config KSU_SUSFS depends on KSU and THREAD_INFO_IN_TASK. The latter is
# already =y in the stock gki_defconfig; KSU is set below.
#
CONFIG_KSU=y
CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS=y
